  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "This storage-only consumer must delegate load/store using node_path\n without resolving contents. Domain requires the callback, but invoking\n this guard would violate the no-content-read invariant of the test.\n Other graph fixtures exercise content resolution."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs` `impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/fn[node_content]` is appropriate.\n\n- **Placement and form:** It is a `cite` in fenced commentary on an explicit function with a body. The function is a guard that only panics, so it is never executed. That is exactly the \"recorded zero execution\" case the built-in exception covers.\n- **Substantive reason:** The commentary says `Domain` requires the callback (the trait declares `fn node_content` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs`). It also says this storage-only fixture must delegate load and store through `node_path` without resolving contents, and that calling the guard would break that invariant. This is more than \"difficulty\".\n- **Agreement with the source:** In `StoredGraph`'s `Domain` impl, `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` delegate to `FileEvidenceStorage` using only `node_path`. `outgoing_edges` is a similar panic guard. The storage tests, such as `consumer_delegates_evidence_storage_using_only_the_requested_nodes_path`, never need content. `StoredReview` ignores its validation context, and `NodeContent` is the uninhabited `UnreadContents`.\n- **Other fixtures:** The claim that other fixtures exercise content resolution holds. Other `Domain` fixtures, such as `Memory` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs`, implement `node_content` and record reads.\n- **No redundancy:** The item has no `impl` or `test` reference to the same target, so no citation is redundant.",
